  "nonObjectTrack": {
    "description": "A stored track whose middle element is not an object. A reader that keeps the stored array (web, Deno) leaves that entry as it is and merges onto the rest, and must not throw: a throw costs it the whole track. The Go writer decodes it as a point with no coordinate, counts it, and places no position on it. The Dart reader cannot hold it in a List<Waypoint>: it drops the entry on decode, and the sidecar, whose point count names the stored array, no longer matches, so expectedDroppingNonObjects is the raw line.",
